                            <comment id="495081" author="JIRAUSER19288" created="Wed, 27 May 2026 16:29:46 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Same for test_24b: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/48905316-c6dc-4987-8f4e-910bad4531a2" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/48905316-c6dc-4987-8f4e-910bad4531a2&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="500652" author="JIRAUSER19288" created="Mon, 31 Aug 2026 08:18:37 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Same for test_1a: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/25f8c3f2-039f-4126-866a-89996ffc5216" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/25f8c3f2-039f-4126-866a-89996ffc5216&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The rc=32 comes from &lt;tt&gt;umount_loopdev()&lt;/tt&gt; which is an EXIT trap defined in &lt;tt&gt;setup_loopdev()&lt;/tt&gt; that is shared by several tests in sanity-pcc, and therefore a bunch of tests can be affected.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
